-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/34606-so-what-happend-with-jesus-and-is-santa-a-changeling?p=37582#post37582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have other Plans for Scion...MWHAHAHAHAHAHA!</div> </div> </div> </div>Santa Christ isn't compatible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-28T13:08:56-08:00","id":38394,"title":"","content":"IIRC trilogy of the fallen implies that god might have sacrificied himself after the fall and became man. or that he lives in every human. so jesus might very well be the &quot;son&quot; of god","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-01T03:33:42-08:00","id":40440,"title":"","content":"There is a Marauder in an official Mage book (the Book of Mirrors or Book of Shadows I think?) named Mr. Nicholas who believed he was Santa Claus. If I recall correctly, he was written in such a way that he could have actually been Santa Clause... except that he didn't have the right Spheres needed to perform a bunch of the traditional miracles.<br /> <br /> As for Jesus, if I were to run him as an element of a game, and interpreted his recorded miracles as literal character capabilities, a very powerful Mage seems like the most obvious choice. I wouldn't tie him to an existing Faction though, especially since he predates any of the formal Traditions by quite some time. However, I'd be <i>really</i> careful before going there. Not because of the type of Christian who'd throw a big stupid martyr-complex hissyfit, but because of the type of Christian who doesn't want to be seen as that first type, but isn't socially savvy or assertive enough to bring up his discomfort more tactfully. That hypothetical guy has enough problems without his friends making jokes about his God being a Malkavian or whatever, and it doesn't take too much effort to double-check if that guy is hiding inside of someone you game with.<br /> <br /> Edit: Then again, playing Demon: the Fallen at all does pretty clearly indicate someone's willing to take liberties with that set of beliefs, so my approach would probably be overly-cautious in your case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please add signature.","edited":{"userid":615,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/615-the-hanged-man","user":"The Hanged Man","date":". 01-01-2014, 03:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/615-the-hanged-man","name":"The Hanged Man","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-01T23:12:21-08:00","id":40933,"title":"","content":"Sorry to contradict, but the Euthanatos and several of their factions predates Christ.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-04T01:22:24-08:00","id":42174,"title":"","content":"In &quot;Bloodline of the Holy Grail&quot; Lawrence Gardner claims that Jesus's brother James helped rescue him from the cross. Interestingly enough no conspiracy theorist I've come across ever mentions the centurion who's servent Jesus saves even though any escape plan would have to include the help of a high level Roman official. Afterwards Jesus traveled to Japan, settled in the Hamlet of Shingo and fathered three children.<br /> <br /> In &quot;Christianity: Origin of a Pagan Relgion&quot; I read that Father Christmas (aka Santa Clause) was origianally a naked hairy fat-man riding on the back of a goat, and he has an adversary named Haraquin; a cadaver dressed in rags riding in a cart pulled by skeleton horses. Haraquin is the spirit of starvation in winter time, Santa Clause is the spirit of the full larder.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1869-moonwolf8","name":"moonwolf8","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-n